:"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZcYKZ5ovoy4"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Murder Ballads (Year not given)","body":null,"year":null,"extra":{"from":"Nick Cave & the Bad Seeds","from_id":96262522505973,"type":"album"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Murder Ballads (and Other Deadly Songs)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FtGJHhqXcDI"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Prominent Relationships (Unspecified Period)","body":"During his lifetime, Michael Hutchence was consistently seen with highly prominent and beautiful women, including film director Michelle Bennett, singer Kylie Minogue, and supermodel Helena Christensen. He also had a relationship with Australian soap opera star Kim Wilson, who was the inspiration for an INXS song. \"When he was alive, he was always in the company of some of the most beautiful women in the world.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Michael Hutchence","from_id":135259033143151,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Tales of Weird Rock’n’Roll Sex","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DA2iJsu3GRY"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Relationship with Helena Christensen","body":"After his relationship with Kylie Minogue ended, he married supermodel Helena Christensen. They resided in a lavish house on five acres in the south of France, where they hosted renowned and beautiful guests from around the world. \"Supermodel Helena Christensen entered the picture. They got married and lived in an incredible house on five acres in the south of France, where they entertained famous and beautiful people from all over the world.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Michael Hutchins","from_id":127014254836151,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Michael Hutchence: 25 Years Later","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=23OgreyK66o"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Relationship with Kylie Minogue","body":"His relationship with Kylie Minogue transformed her public image from a \"mild-mannered pop star\" to a \"supervixen dude.\" He openly stated his hobby was \"corrupting her.\" Tabloids frequently reported on their relationship, including stories about customs finding handcuffs and other devices in her luggage, all-night ecstasy binges, and embarrassing nightclub moments. Kylie was also allegedly the inspiration for a song after expressing a desire to dye her hair. \"Michael even admitted that his hobby was, quote, corrupting her.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Michael Hutchins","from_id":127014254836151,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Michael Hutchence: 25 Years Later","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=23OgreyK66o"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Relationships and Early Promiscuity","body":"He was known for dating some of the world's most beautiful women, making him a tabloid favorite. His partners included Virginia Hey (a Bond girl), Belinda Carlisle (The Go-Go's singer), and Kylie Minogue. From the age of 15, women were a \"real weakness,\" with early touring days sometimes involving sex with three women a night in the band's panel van. \"He went out with Virginia Hay, a bond girl from the living daylights. He went out with Blinda Carlyle, the singer of the Go-Gos. Singer Kylie Minogue was a partner for a while.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Michael Hutchins","from_id":127014254836151,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Michael Hutchence: 25 Years Later","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=23OgreyK66o"}]}],"charts":[{"id":167319966332202,"type":"song","name":"The Loco-Motion","work_year":1988,"list_id":162518251001675,"list":"Billboard Year-End 1988","src":"singles","rank":49,"year":1988,"note":"","yt":"POWsFzSFLCE","scaruffi":null},{"id":167319966332202,"type":"song","name":"The Loco-Motion","work_year":1988,"list_id":132335824845498,"list":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","src":"charts","rank":49,"year":1988,"